   "html_text": "Like NSM and Conceptual Semantics, Two-Level Semantics associates word meanings with stable decompositional templates. At the same time, by allowing SFs to interface with world knowledge, it avoids the immediate hindrances of a restrictive account of the factors that can modulate the decompositional templates in contexts. Some issues, however, persist. A first problem is, again, definitional accuracy for semantically close terms: the SF ⟦M⟧ assigned to ‘university’ would work equally well as the",
